# Model registry for the four-arm cell. Loaded automatically by
# core/decision/model_registry.py.
#
# NO SECRETS IN THIS FILE. It lives inside the project tree and therefore
# ends up inside every zip. Each alias names the ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE that
# carries its key (<ALIAS>_KEY_VAR); the key itself is exported from your
# shell and never written down here.
#
# A real environment variable always wins over a line in this file, so
# existing exports keep working and a one-off override needs no edit.
#
# Adding a model is four lines: add its name to FOURARM_MODELS, then give
# it ENDPOINT, MODEL, KEY_VAR and PARAMS.

FOURARM_MODELS=qwen,gpt,gemini,claude

# Which alias is used when nothing asks for one. Keeps every existing
# command, harness and episode on the model they already ran against.
FOURARM_MODEL=qwen


# --- qwen ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alibaba DashScope, international compatible-mode endpoint.
# temperature 0.0 is what every episode up to 2026-08-01 was run with, so it
# stays here rather than being hardcoded in the client.
QWEN_ENDPOINT=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions
QWEN_MODEL=qwen-vl-max
QWEN_KEY_VAR=QWEN_API_KEY
QWEN_PARAMS={"temperature": 0.0}


# --- gpt -------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI, the cross-lineage contrast model. Verified against the live
# endpoint 2026-08-01: /v1/chat/completions accepts gpt-5.6-terra and
# returns the usual choices[0].message.content.
#
# reasoning_effort is pinned LOW on purpose. qwen-vl-max has no test-time
# reasoning, so running this model at a higher effort would compare model
# families AND test-time compute at the same time, and the two-model claim
# exists precisely to separate confounds rather than add one. Higher effort
# is a separate stamped condition, not a default.
#
# temperature is deliberately absent: the GPT-5.x reasoning tiers reject a
# non-default value, and the empty slot is more honest than a value that is
# silently ignored. Determinism is therefore NOT comparable across the two
# aliases, which is a limitation to state, not a bug to hide.
GPT_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
GPT_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
GPT_KEY_VAR=OPENAI_API_KEY
GPT_PARAMS={"reasoning_effort": "low"}


# --- gemini ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Google, via the OpenAI compatibility shim. The trailing /openai/ segment
# maps the OpenAI wire format onto Gemini's own API, so /chat/completions
# under that base is a drop-in and openai_chat needs no change. The key is a
# standard Gemini API key passed as a Bearer token; an OpenAI key will not
# work here.
#
# Pro rather than Flash on purpose. The comparison is between capable
# models, and a fast cheap tier landing between gpt and qwen would be
# uninterpretable: a middling score could mean either the family behaves
# differently or the tier is simply weaker.
#
# VERIFY THE MODEL STRING before the first paid run. Google's naming has
# moved twice in 2026 and the docs currently show gemini-3.5-flash as stable
# with gemini-3.6-flash in the compatibility examples, so the Pro string
# below is the thing most likely to be stale in this file. Check
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models and correct it here rather
# than in a command.
#
# No temperature. Reasoning cannot be disabled on the Gemini 3 generation,
# so this alias behaves like gpt (test-time reasoning, no temperature
# control) rather than like qwen (temperature 0.0, no reasoning). That makes
# determinism non-comparable across all three families, which is a
# limitation to state rather than a knob to force.
GEMINI_ENDPOINT=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/chat/completions
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
GEMINI_KEY_VAR=GEMINI_API_KEY
GEMINI_PARAMS={}


# --- claude ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic. NOTE: the native Anthropic API is NOT OpenAI-shaped. It uses
# /v1/messages, an x-api-key header rather than Bearer, a required
# anthropic-version header, and it returns content blocks rather than
# choices[0].message.content. openai_chat will fail against it.
#
# So this alias must point at an OpenAI-compatible gateway, or at Bedrock or
# Vertex through their OpenAI-compatible surfaces. The endpoint below is a
# PLACEHOLDER and will not work until it names a real gateway.
#
# claude-opus-5 rather than claude-fable-5: Fable is the top tier but only
# became generally available on 2026-06-09, and Opus 5 is the more standard
# reference point. Model IDs from the 4.6 generation onward are pinned, so
# a dateless id maps to one fixed snapshot and will not drift mid-experiment.
CLAUDE_ENDPOINT=REPLACE_WITH_OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_GATEWAY/chat/completions
CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5
CLAUDE_KEY_VAR=ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
CLAUDE_PARAMS={}